1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,605
Get ready for the highest continuous paved road in America!

2
00:00:06,605 --> 00:00:12,181
Eleven miles above treeline, topping out at twelve thousand one hundred eighty-three feet.

3
00:00:12,181 --> 00:00:16,022
The highest visitor center in the whole National Park Service.

4
00:00:16,022 --> 00:00:19,430
And Colorado's biggest natural lake waiting at the end!

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:27,532
This is Trail Ridge Road: 48 miles across Rocky Mountain National Park, right over the top of the Rockies.

6
00:00:27,532 --> 00:00:31,040
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,080
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:45,550
We leave Estes Park, climb to Many Parks Curve and Forest Canyon Overlook, stop at the Alpine Visitor Center, cross the Continental Divide at Milner Pass, and roll down to Grand Lake!

9
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,765
We're starting in Estes Park, the gateway to Rocky Mountain National Park!

10
00:00:51,765 --> 00:00:57,885
Fun fact: the Stanley Hotel up on the hill inspired Stephen King to write The Shining.

11
00:00:57,885 --> 00:00:58,383
Spooky!

12
00:00:58,383 --> 00:00:59,450
Okay, let's go!

13
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:07,261
We roll into Rocky Mountain National Park through the Beaver Meadows Entrance, and the climb starts right away!

14
00:01:07,261 --> 00:01:12,330
This road was built back in the early 1930s, and it still feels like an adventure!

15
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:15,176
Welcome to Many Parks Curve!

16
00:01:15,176 --> 00:01:21,878
In Colorado, a park is a big mountain meadow, and from this boardwalk you can spot a bunch of them.

17
00:01:21,878 --> 00:01:23,570
Watch for elk down below!

18
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,457
Next up, Rainbow Curve, at nearly eleven thousand feet.

19
00:01:28,457 --> 00:01:31,177
Pull over, because the views are huge!

20
00:01:31,177 --> 00:01:37,835
Then we pop up above treeline, where about eleven miles of this road cross the alpine tundra.

21
00:01:37,835 --> 00:01:40,340
It feels like the top of the world!

22
00:01:41,290 --> 00:01:46,096
This is Forest Canyon Overlook, eleven thousand seven hundred feet!

23
00:01:46,096 --> 00:01:49,037
Take the short walk out to the viewpoint.

24
00:01:49,037 --> 00:01:55,780
Glaciers carved this canyon, and those jagged peaks across the way are the Continental Divide!

25
00:01:56,730 --> 00:01:58,159
Now for the big one!

26
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:04,517
Stretch your legs on the Tundra Communities Trail at Rock Cut, and say hi to the marmots.

27
00:02:04,517 --> 00:02:11,304
Then we hit the highest point on the whole road, twelve thousand one hundred eighty-three feet!

28
00:02:11,304 --> 00:02:15,090
This is the highest continuous paved road in America!

29
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:21,216
Welcome to the Alpine Visitor Center, eleven thousand seven hundred ninety-six feet!

30
00:02:21,216 --> 00:02:25,344
It's the highest visitor center in the whole National Park Service.

31
00:02:25,344 --> 00:02:29,780
Grab a snack, then climb the Alpine Ridge Trail for an even bigger view!

32
00:02:30,730 --> 00:02:33,962
From here it's downhill to the Continental Divide!

33
00:02:33,962 --> 00:02:36,160
At Medicine Bow Curve, look north.

34
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:40,750
Those are the Medicine Bow Mountains, running all the way into Wyoming!

35
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:47,951
Milner Pass, ten thousand seven hundred fifty-eight feet, right on the Continental Divide!

36
00:02:47,951 --> 00:02:49,270
That's Poudre Lake.

37
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:55,660
Its water flows east toward the Atlantic, and everything west of here heads for the Pacific!

38
00:02:56,610 --> 00:03:00,075
Now we switchback down into the Kawuneeche Valley!

39
00:03:00,075 --> 00:03:08,253
Stop at Farview Curve for a view of the Never Summer Mountains, then visit Holzwarth Historic Site, an old dude ranch.

40
00:03:08,253 --> 00:03:10,748
And keep your eyes peeled for moose!

41
00:03:10,748 --> 00:03:14,490
The Colorado River starts right here as a tiny stream!

42
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,064
Welcome to Grand Lake!

43
00:03:17,064 --> 00:03:23,413
It's Colorado's largest natural lake, with a wooden boardwalk town right on the shore.

44
00:03:23,413 --> 00:03:27,326
Rent a boat, grab an ice cream, and watch the sunset.

45
00:03:27,326 --> 00:03:28,360
What a finish!

46
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:31,786
And that's Trail Ridge Road!

47
00:03:31,786 --> 00:03:37,710
48 miles from Estes Park to Grand Lake, topping out at 12,183 feet.

48
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:41,820
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

49
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,590
Pause and grab a screenshot!

50
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,971
Thanks for riding along!

51
00:03:48,971 --> 00:03:54,630
Hit subscribe, and next time we're heading over Independence Pass to Aspen!
